  {
    "sha": "6019b702569cb38343ebc70dff4a6d6a883c4904",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOPf6Nn9oAKDYwMTliNzAyNTY5Y2IzODM0M2ViYzcwZGZmNGE2ZDZhODgzYzQ5MDQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "asmo",
        "email": "asmogo@protonmail.com",
        "date": "2026-05-22T08:35:21Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "asmo",
        "email": "asmogo@protonmail.com",
        "date": "2026-05-22T08:35:21Z"
      },
      "message": "fix: pass --config to uniffi-bindgen so Swift module name is CashuDevKit\n\nThe xcframework build started failing in CI with:\n\n    mv: rename Sources/CashuDevKit/CashuDevKitFFI.h to \\\n        ../cdk/target/include/CashuDevKitFFI.h: No such file or directory\n\nRoot cause: in uniffi 0.30 library mode the per-crate uniffi.toml is not\nauto-discovered. The Swift module name comes from\ncrates/cdk-ffi/uniffi.toml (module_name = \"CashuDevKit\"). uniffi resolves\nwhich config to use by the crate's lib target name, but the cdk workspace\nnow contains two crates whose lib target is named `cdk_ffi`\n(crates/cdk-ffi and bindings/kotlin/rust, the latter renamed from\ncdk_ffi_kotlin in cdk commit 9f6cd097). That collision makes the namespace\nlookup ambiguous, so module_name is dropped and bindgen emits\ncdk_ffiFFI.h instead of CashuDevKitFFI.h — and the subsequent `mv` fails.\n\nPassing --config explicitly pins the Swift bindings config regardless of\nthe collision, restoring CashuDevKit* output. Applied to both\nbuild-xcframework.sh (cwd = cdk root) and generate-bindings.sh\n(cwd = cdk-ffi crate dir).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "014c4da739e57e63b2ac7aae48211ae7b3f0a8a1",
